WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.075
"We can't open the wormhole again without magic!" Gliss exclaimed. "We could be trapped here forever!"

2
00:00:08.076 --> 00:00:09.071
Crash

3
00:00:09.072 --> 00:00:12.187
! Zann spun around as something landed behind

4
00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:15.523
them. It was a large platter of puckerberry

5
00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:21.071
pancakes! "The food!" Darb said. "It's here. I guess the spell worked after

6
00:00:21.072 --> 00:00:29.379
all." "It just took a long time." Perda stuck her finger in the pancake syrup and licked it.

7
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:34.108
"Mmm!" "It's weird that the spell took so long to work," Zann

8
00:00:34.109 --> 00:00:38.115
said. "We should try another spell and see if the same thing

9
00:00:38.116 --> 00:00:42.496
happens." "I'll do it." Perda rubbed her hands together.

10
00:00:42.497 --> 00:00:50.557
"Levitate!" They all waited. Several moments passed before Perda's feet finally lifted off the

11
00:00:50.558 --> 00:00:54.577
ground. "Magic must work really slowly here, that's

12
00:00:54.578 --> 00:00:57.441
all." Zann stepped toward the wormhole and

13
00:00:57.442 --> 00:01:03.639
waited. Eventually it swirled open again. "Phew! We're not trapped after

14
00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:09.881
all." "Good." Perda reached for a pancake. "Let's eat, and then we can look for

15
00:01:09.882 --> 00:01:13.784
Wyssa." Darb peered into the distance. "Someone's

16
00:01:13.785 --> 00:01:16.871
coming." Several people were moving slowly toward

17
00:01:16.872 --> 00:01:22.058
them. They were very slim and tall, with extra-long arms and

18
00:01:22.059 --> 00:01:27.759
legs. Their skin, hair, and clothes were the same dull colors as the rest of their

19
00:01:27.760 --> 00:01:32.092
world. "Should we run away or stay and talk to them?" Gliss

20
00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:39.473
asked. "They look pretty friendly," Perda said. "Besides, I'm guessing we can outrun them if we have

21
00:01:39.474 --> 00:01:43.266
to." Several minutes later the natives reached the

22
00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:54.670
visitors. "Greetings, strangers," one of them said. His voice was slow but friendly. "Welcome to

23
00:01:54.671 --> 00:01:59.285
Chronos." "Thank you," Zann said. "We just arrived through the

24
00:01:59.286 --> 00:02:03.271
wormhole." "Is everything always so slow here?" Perda

25
00:02:03.272 --> 00:02:08.298
asked. Long-drawn-out chuckles emerged from several of the

26
00:02:08.299 --> 00:02:15.159
Chronians. "That's the first question every visitor asks," said one

27
00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:22.823
Chronian. "Yes, time moves more slowly here than it does in most other

28
00:02:22.824 --> 00:02:40.352
worlds." "That's right," another Chronian continued. "For every hour that passes in Chronos, just seconds pass in the vortex or most other

29
00:02:40.353 --> 00:02:44.555
worlds." Zann already felt impatient with the Chronians' slow

30
00:02:44.556 --> 00:02:50.703
speech. "Has anyone else visited lately?" he asked. "A woman named

31
00:02:50.704 --> 00:03:09.590
Wyssa?" "Yes," one of the Chronians said. "Wyssa arrived here earlier. But she moved on

32
00:03:09.591 --> 00:03:12.712
immediately." Zann frowned. Their tracking method was

33
00:03:12.713 --> 00:03:15.631
working. But they couldn't seem to catch up with

34
00:03:15.632 --> 00:03:18.859
Wyssa! "Do you know where she was going next?" he

35
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:23.550
asked. "Was it a place called World X? A newly discovered

36
00:03:23.551 --> 00:03:31.028
world?" "Wyssa wasn't here long enough to tell us about her plans," a Chronian

37
00:03:31.029 --> 00:03:40.148
said. Another Chronian spoke up. "Wait—Wyssa might not have said

38
00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:48.146
anything. But a traveler who passed by a few days ago did mention a new

39
00:03:48.147 --> 00:03:55.738
world." "Really?" Zann spun to face him. "Was the traveler a tall, skinny guy named

40
00:03:55.739 --> 00:04:02.575
Morb?" "No." A look of confusion passed slowly over the Chronian's

41
00:04:02.576 --> 00:04:09.112
face. "It was a trader who passes through Chronos

42
00:04:09.113 --> 00:04:13.811
frequently. He visits many worlds in his

43
00:04:13.812 --> 00:04:17.004
travels." "What did he say?" Zann's heart pounded.

44
00:04:17.005 --> 00:04:20.236
Could this be the clue that would lead to his parents?

45
00:04:20.237 --> 00:04:23.387
Maybe they wouldn't need to catch Wyssa after all!

46
00:04:23.388 --> 00:04:28.324
"The trader has heard rumors," the Chronian said.

47
00:04:28.325 --> 00:04:41.281
"Supposedly there's a world with wormholes that lead not only into the vortex, but directly into other worlds as well!"

48
00:04:41.282 --> 00:04:44.995
"But that's not how wormholes work," Perda said.

49
00:04:44.996 --> 00:04:49.892
"You have to travel through the vortex to go from one world to another."

50
00:04:49.893 --> 00:04:58.209
The Chronian shrugged. "I know. The trader wasn't sure it was true either.

51
00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:03.494
He hasn't seen this strange world himself."

52
00:05:03.495 --> 00:05:07.716
"If it's real, it could be World X," Zann said.

53
00:05:07.717 --> 00:05:12.038
"It sure sounds like the kind of place that my parents would want to find."

54
00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:15.126
He glanced at his friends. "We should go!"

55
00:05:15.127 --> 00:05:18.789
Perda yawned and reached for another pancake.

56
00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.868
"Why don't we rest here for a little while first?

57
00:05:22.869 --> 00:05:30.280
You heard what they said—even if we stay here for hours, only a few seconds will pass everywhere else."

58
00:05:30.281 --> 00:05:35.173
Zann wanted to argue, but he could see that his friends were hungry and tired.

59
00:05:35.174 --> 00:05:41.154
"All right," he said. "But let's make it a short rest, okay?"

60
00:05:41.155 --> 00:05:44.710
The Chronians led them to a gray town nearby.

61
00:05:44.711 --> 00:05:51.095
The local innkeeper offered the visitors food and drink, which was nearly tasteless but filling.

62
00:05:51.096 --> 00:05:55.283
Then she showed Zann and his friends to comfortable beds.

63
00:05:55.284 --> 00:05:58.332
Zann was sure he'd never be able to sleep.

64
00:05:58.333 --> 00:06:02.535
But he drifted off quickly and fell into another vivid dream.

65
00:06:02.536 --> 00:06:08.816
His parents were running in terror through a forest with dark magic swirling around them.

66
00:06:08.817 --> 00:06:12.938
Like everything else in Chronos, the dream moved slowly.

67
00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:17.795
That gave Zann time to see details he hadn't noticed in his previous dreams.

68
00:06:17.796 --> 00:06:24.008
In the forest there were tiny houses with doors no higher than his mother's knee.

69
00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:30.091
While the forest seemed dark, the sky overhead was a brilliant shade of blue.

70
00:06:30.092 --> 00:06:34.075
Zann finally awoke, blinking in the pale gray light.

71
00:06:34.076 --> 00:06:38.185
Could anything in his dream be a clue to finding his parents?

72
00:06:38.186 --> 00:06:44.444
Lots of worlds had blue skies. But not many worlds had such tiny houses.

73
00:06:44.445 --> 00:06:49.436
Even Fud from Galvan was too big to fit through those small doors.

74
00:06:49.437 --> 00:06:52.543
Eager to get moving, Zann woke his friends.

75
00:06:52.544 --> 00:06:57.097
It seemed to take forever for the Chronians to guide them back to the wormhole.

76
00:06:57.098 --> 00:07:03.013
Then Zann had to wait for the mutual shackles to appear, and for the wormhole to open.

77
00:07:03.014 --> 00:07:06.924
But finally he and his friends were back in the vortex.

78
00:07:06.925 --> 00:07:10.981
"Wow," Gliss said as wormholes rushed past.

79
00:07:10.982 --> 00:07:15.684
"It feels weird to be living at full speed again."

80
00:07:15.685 --> 00:07:20.948
"Yeah." Darb looked at Zann. "Hey, the purple mark is glowing!"

81
00:07:20.949 --> 00:07:26.153
"Good." Zann grabbed the next wormhole and pulled his friends through.

82
00:07:26.154 --> 00:07:34.195
The world they landed in was dark, with jagged lightning splitting the sky. Zann recognized it and gasped.

83
00:07:34.196 --> 00:07:44.864
Apparently Perda recognized it too. "Oh no! We're back in Fardark!"

